  "asserted_semantics": [
    "Definitions are object-local and bounded; a larger curve is a budget refusal rather than a truncated definition.",
    "NURBS reports degree, poles, weights, knots, domain, periodic, reversed and seam; a circle reports its optional arc angle domain; a polycurve reports its segment count.",
    "closed = distance(first, last) <= tolerance on the owner's 33-sample curve; planar uses the owner's Newell-normal rule; the tolerance used is reported back.",
    "A document that states no tolerance refuses the implicit measurement; the caller must pass an explicit tolerance instead of receiving an invented default.",
    "A curve whose sampled length is at or below the tolerance is refused as degenerate, never reclassified.",
    "Reading a definition or semantics stages no mutation."
  ],
